4. Python's textwrap module (https://github.com/python/cpython, Lib/textwrap.py)

The port was made from Lib/textwrap.py of Python 3.12, the Python that runs
datamapplot in the Delphi image; that file is the same in every 3.12 release
from v3.12.0. Its copyright notices:

  Copyright (C) 1999-2001 Gregory P. Ward.
  Copyright (C) 2002, 2003 Python Software Foundation.
  Written by Greg Ward <gward@python.net>

datamapplot wraps a label with Python's textwrap.fill(text, width,
break_long_words=False). wrapLabel in topic-map.js ports it: WORDSEP is
TextWrapper.wordsep_re written as a JavaScript regular expression, and the
loop that fills lines is TextWrapper._wrap_chunks for that one setting. Summary
of the changes: translated from Python to JavaScript; only the path for
break_long_words=False, with TextWrapper's other defaults and no indent,
placeholder or line limit, is kept; Python's word and letter classes are
written as Unicode property classes; a tab becomes one space rather than
spaces to the next tab stop; in the second look-behind for a hyphenated word
(letter, hyphen, letter, hyphen in Python), the character after the first
hyphen is matched by the class of word characters and punctuation.

