6. The public fixtures (test/fixtures/)

Two public conversations from https://github.com/compdemocracy/openData,
licensed CC BY 4.0: bg2050-volunteers and scoop-hivemind.biodiversity. Data was
gathered using the Polis software (see: compdemocracy.org/polis and
github.com/compdemocracy/polis) and is sub-licensed under CC BY 4.0 with
Attribution to The Computational Democracy Project.

- biodiversity.topic-map.json is the polis-topic-map/1 document of one Delphi
  run of scoop-hivemind.biodiversity (154 comments moderated in, of 316): the
  comments' positions (embeddings all-MiniLM-L6-v2, UMAP), their topics at two
  levels (EVoC clustering) and the comments' text. Its topic names were written
  by a small local model (qwen2.5:1.5b) and are not the names pol.is shows. Its
  topic colours were computed from the CET-C2s colour map (colorcet 3.1.0;
  Peter Kovesi, "Good Colour Maps: How to Design Them", arXiv:1509.03700,
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License).
- datamapplot-labels.json holds, for one Delphi run of each of the two
  conversations, the topic names by level and the label strings datamapplot
  0.6.4 made of them; nothing else.
